{
  // The axe's side swing and the permanent chop damage at the oak trees.json films (full-thickness
  // trunk cell at (-79, 14, -2), hardness 24, so the primitive axe's 1.0 per 0.3 s takes about 7 s): run
  // with VOXEL_SCRIPT=visual-examples/animations-axe.json VOXEL_TIME=147 from OpenGLTest/. Shots land
  // in visual/animations-axe/. The player hovers while the chunks load, then drops to the ground and
  // stands in survival 2.5 blocks south of the trunk facing it and really mines it, so each hit shows
  // the side swing, the chips off the trunk, the camera nudge and a few leaves shaken loose from the
  // crown. The face being hit is eaten away from the viewer's left to the right as the damage builds
  // (instead of the crack overlay), and it stays eaten: bite_kept is taken after letting go. The wind-up
  // starts ahead of each hit, so every shot after the first hit catches the blade on its way across as
  // the hit lands. Shots are approximate (a frame or two after their wait); the last one is the trunk
  // after the tree came down.
  "steps": [
    { "op": "fly" },
    { "op": "teleport", "pos": [-78.5, 15.7, -4.5], "yaw": 90, "pitch": -5 },
